# Git history during new-functionality implementation

While implementing new functionality, explore only the working tree and history
reachable from `HEAD`. Do not inspect code from other refs as a source or reference.

This restriction does not apply:

- outside implementation of new functionality, such as review, diagnosis, comparison,
  release investigation, maintenance, or git operations;
- when the user explicitly asks to inspect, compare, reuse, port, or merge another ref.

## Restricted during new-functionality implementation

- Other local or remote branches, tags, stashes, reflogs, and PR branches
- Ref-wide searches such as `git log --all`, `--branches`, or `--remotes`
- `git fetch` performed only to discover implementation code
- Remote branch or PR code read through the `gh` CLI or GitHub MCP

```bash
# ❌ BAD — discovering implementation code on another ref
git log --all --oneline
git show origin/prototype:src/new-module.ts

# ✅ GOOD — implement from requirements and the current tree
git status
git log --oneline -n 20
```

If another branch may contain related work, do not inspect it. Mention its name to the
parent or user so they can explicitly authorize using it.
